<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Holy League (1571)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1571">1571</a>–<a href="/years/1573">1573</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Holy League of 1571 was an alliance against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> formed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-v">Pope Pius V</a> with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genoa">Genoa</a>, Savoy, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights of Malta</a> and other Italian states. Its fleet, commanded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-austria">Don John of Austria</a>, destroyed the Ottoman navy at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-lepanto">Battle of Lepanto</a> in October 1571. The alliance soon broke up, and Venice made a separate peace in 1573, ceding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyprus">Cyprus</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/holy-league-1571.jpg" alt="Holy League (1571)" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rafael Monleón · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Estandarte_Liga_Santa.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
